---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const quickStart = `import * as nn from "typenn";

const device = await nn.device();
const input = device.tensor([1, 2, 3, 4], { shape: [2, 2] });
const weight = device.tensor([5, 6, 7, 8], { shape: [2, 2] });
const output = input.matmul(weight).relu();

console.log(await output.data());
// Float32Array [19, 22, 43, 50]
await output.disposeGraph();
await device.dispose();`;
---

<SiteLayout locale="en" active="home" title="TypeNN — Neural networks in TypeScript" description="Write Tensor operations in TypeScript, run them through the TypeShade compiler and runtime, and try the framework in your browser.">
  <div class="home-content">
    <section class="home-intro">
      <div class="home-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A TypeScript neural network framework</p>
        <h1>Write the graph.<br /><span>Compile the work.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">TypeNN gives Tensor and Module code a deferred graph. TypeShade compiles its kernels and executes them on CPU and supported GPU backends.</p>
        <div class="action-row">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/playground/">Try the playground <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="button button-quiet" href="/guide/">Read the guide</a>
        </div>
        <p class="release-note">Pre-release · source and examples are the current usage reference.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="home-code">
        <CodeBlock title="Tensor API" file="example.ts" code={quickStart} />
        <div class="execution-result"><span class="result-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Float32Array</span><code>[19, 22, 43, 50]</code><span class="result-label">Example output</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-path" aria-labelledby="path-title">
      <div class="section-heading-row">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">From TypeScript to execution</p><h2 id="path-title">Three layers, one visible path.</h2></div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/guide/execution/">How execution works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="path-strip">
        <article><span class="path-index">01</span><h3>Define</h3><p>Tensor calls describe shapes and operations. TypeNN records them as graph nodes.</p><code>tensor.matmul(weight).relu()</code></article>
        <article><span class="path-index">02</span><h3>Lower</h3><p>TypeNN maps graph operations to its TypeShade kernel programs.</p><code>Tensor graph → kernel program</code></article>
        <article><span class="path-index">03</span><h3>Run</h3><p>TypeShade dispatches the reachable work on the selected execution tier.</p><code>CPU · WebGPU · WebGL2*</code></article>
      </div>
      <p class="fine-print">* WebGL2 uses a constrained compute lowering path. A Frame can group dispatches; that does not mean the kernels are fused.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-learning" aria-labelledby="learn-title">
      <div class="learning-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Explore TypeNN</p><h2 id="learn-title">Start with a runnable operation. Continue into the system.</h2><p>Try matrix operations in the browser, then follow the guide into graph execution, automatic differentiation, and model training.</p></div>
      <div class="learning-links">
        <a href="/playground/"><span><strong>Playground</strong><small>Run real TypeNN operations in this browser.</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>
        <a href="/guide/training/"><span><strong>Train a model</strong><small>Build the documented MNIST MLP path.</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>
        <a href="/api/"><span><strong>API reference</strong><small>Browse the current Tensor and Module surface.</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>
        <a href="/examples/"><span><strong>Examples</strong><small>Open complete source examples and current limits.</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Current implementation</p><h2 id="status-title">The framework is compiler-first. Its optimizer is still evolving.</h2><p>GPU training keeps gradients and Adam state resident and updates parameters through TypeShade kernels. Tensor graph operations still dispatch separately; graph-wide fusion and tiled MatMul remain future work.</p></div>
      <a class="button button-quiet" href="https://github.com/typeshade/typenn/blob/main/TODO.md">Read implementation status <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
